{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0283","billNumberShort":"S.B. 283","billNumberLong":"SB0283S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0220","shortTitle":"Court Fees and Administration Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"WEILET","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Weiler, Todd","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"MILLGR","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Miller, Grant Amjad","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies provisions related to fees and various administrative procedures of the court system.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>removes obsolete provisions:<hr><ltbullet1>allowing a sheriff to appoint a law school graduate as a bailiff;<hr><ltbullet1>requiring the Judicial Council to create a fine schedule for juvenile courts; and<hr><ltbullet1>relating to the use of revenue from court fees to fund court building projects;<hr><ltbullet>updates terminology;<hr><ltbullet>provides that all civil document fees for justice courts and courts of record are provided at no charge to the state, state agencies, or political subdivisions;<hr><ltbullet>increases certain court fees;<hr><ltbullet>requires the Administrative Office of the Courts to use appropriated funds from the Court Security Account to contract for court security at all courts of record; <hr><ltbullet>provides that a request for a protective order does not have a filing fee surcharge under the Online Court Assistance Program; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Paige Nelson","fiscalAnalyst":"Gary R. Syphus","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/23/2026","trackingID":"XCJFXEINDC","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-02-10 14:20:03.670","actionClass":"L","vot